# ============================================================================
# NOTE: this single-file script is SUPERSEDED by the modular pipeline in
# NEPC-scRNA-clustering-pipeline/ (v2.0: Harmony integration, doublet removal,
# UCell scoring, and the integrated stromal tier for ASPC). It is kept for
# reference only and is no longer updated.
# ============================================================================
# ============================================================================
# 07_ NEPC scRNA-seq: per-dataset clustering + cell-population annotation,
#     recurrent populations across datasets, and correlation of their
#     signatures with the NEPC (Beltran, custom UP) signature in bulk
#     RNA-seq from PRAD TCGA and prad_su2c_2019 (cBioPortal)
# ============================================================================
#
# INPUT  — seven NEPC dataset folders (one folder = one dataset):
#   /Volumes/Jingjing_Chen/NEPC scRNA dataset/GSE137829         human
#   /Volumes/Jingjing_Chen/NEPC scRNA dataset/GSE210358         human
#   /Volumes/Jingjing_Chen/NEPC scRNA dataset/GSE210358_TKO     mouse
#   /Volumes/Jingjing_Chen/NEPC scRNA dataset/GSE235036_TKO     mouse
#   /Volumes/Jingjing_Chen/NEPC scRNA dataset/GSE264573         human
#   /Volumes/Jingjing_Chen/NEPC scRNA dataset/GSE292074         human
#   /Volumes/Jingjing_Chen/NEPC scRNA dataset/GSE296986_TKO     mouse
#
# PART 1 — per dataset (all samples in the folder are MERGED into one object)
#   1. Scan the folder for samples: a 10x triplet (<s>_barcodes.tsv.gz +
#      <s>_features.tsv.gz + <s>_matrix.mtx.gz) or ONE file per sample
#      (<s>.txt.gz | <s>.csv.gz | <s>.zip | <s>.matrix.zip | <s>.tar.gz);
#      every other file in the folder is ignored
#   2. Load each sample; per-cell QC (min features, mitochondrial %)
#   3. Merge -> NormalizeData -> HVGs -> ScaleData -> PCA -> SNN graph ->
#      Louvain clustering -> UMAP            (unsupervised clustering)
#   4. FindAllMarkers for every cluster
#   5. Cell-subpopulation annotation of every cluster, two independent layers:
#        (a) PRIMARY  — canonical marker-panel scoring (POPULATION_MARKERS):
#            cluster-level mean log-normalised expression of each panel gene,
#            z-scored across clusters, averaged per panel; the best-scoring
#            panel names the cluster ("Unassigned" if score/margin too low)
#        (b) SECONDARY — SingleR per-cell reference labels (celldex
#            HumanPrimaryCellAtlas / MouseRNAseq) summarised to the majority
#            label per cluster
#   6. Outputs -> <dataset folder>/07_clustering/
#
# PART 2 — recurrent populations
#   Every annotated population is counted across datasets. Populations seen in
#   MORE THAN cfg$recurrence_min_datasets datasets (default 3, i.e. >= 4 of 7)
#   are listed in 07_recurrent_populations.csv. Counting by cluster occurrences
#   instead of datasets is available via cfg$recurrence_count_by.
#
# PART 3 — correlation with the NEPC signature in bulk cohorts
#   For every recurrent population two signatures are built:
#        canonical         the known marker panel used for annotation
#        consensus_markers data-derived markers of that population recurring
#                          in >= cfg$consensus_min_datasets datasets
#   Bulk mRNA expression is fetched from the cBioPortal REST API for
#   prad_tcga and prad_su2c_2019 (local datahub files can be used instead via
#   cfg$cbio_local_files). Per sample: log2(x + 1) -> gene-wise z-score ->
#   signature score = mean z over signature genes. Each population score is
#   correlated (Pearson + Spearman) with the NEPC score across samples; every
#   signature gene is also correlated individually with the NEPC score.
#   Outputs -> <NEPC_ROOT>/07_cross_dataset/
#
# REQUIRED PACKAGES
#   Seurat (>= 4; v5 layers handled), SingleR, celldex, SingleCellExperiment,
#   Matrix, data.table, dplyr, tidyr, tibble, stringr, ggplot2, patchwork,
#   httr, jsonlite. (hdf5r only if a dataset ships .h5 matrices.)
#
# RE-RUNNING
#   Set cfg$run_part1 / run_part2 / run_part3. Part 1 is skipped for a dataset
#   whose 07_clustering/07_seurat_annotated.rds already exists when
#   cfg$reuse_existing = TRUE. Parts 2 and 3 only read Part 1 outputs.
# ============================================================================

